**Requirement ID:** KKCOMM-15313

**Test Case:** FRM-14706 - Request to Destroy - Field Configuration

**Step 1**

**Description:**
Log in as a System Administrator, record the URL and User Name, and navigate to Setup.

**Expected Result:**
Setup should be displayed successfully.

---

**Step 2**

**Description:**
Navigate to Object Manager > Treatment Case > Fields & Relationships. Verify the availability of the Name field associated with Cancellation Requested By (KK_Cancellation_Requested_By__c). Open the field and verify the Data Type and Description under Field Information.

**Expected Result:**
The Name field should be available and configured as a lookup to store the contact who requested final product destruction.

The Description should be displayed as:

"[Confidential] - Stores a lookup to the contact who requested a final product destruction".

---

**Step 3**

**Description:**
Navigate back to Fields & Relationships. Verify the availability of the Role field associated with Cancellation Requested By (KK_Cancellation_Requested_By_Role__c). Open the field and verify the Data Type and Description under Field Information.

**Expected Result:**
The Role field should be available and configured as a free-text field.

The Description should be displayed as:

"[Confidential] - Stores the role of the contact who requested a final product destruction".

---

**Step 4**

**Description:**
Navigate back to Fields & Relationships and click Set History Tracking. Verify the Field History Tracking settings for the Name and Role fields associated with Cancellation Requested By.

**Expected Result:**
Field History Tracking should be disabled for both fields.

---

**Step 5**

**Description:**
Navigate back to Fields & Relationships. Open the Name field associated with Cancellation Requested By and click Set Field-Level Security. Verify the profile-level access.

**Expected Result:**
Profile-level access for the Name field should be configured as follows:

- System Admin: Read, Edit
- System Admin Support: Read, Edit
- System Admin Deployments: Read
- Case Managers: Read, Edit
- Logistics: N/A
- Site Quality: Read
- System Support: Read
- Read Only Case Manager: Read
- Read Only Logistics: N/A
- Accession: N/A
- Integration: N/A
- HCP: N/A
- HCP Restricted: N/A
- Referring Physician: N/A

---

**Step 6**

**Description:**
Navigate back to Fields & Relationships. Open the Role field associated with Cancellation Requested By and click Set Field-Level Security. Verify the profile-level access.

**Expected Result:**
Profile-level access for the Role field should be configured as follows:

- System Admin: Read, Edit
- System Admin Support: Read, Edit
- System Admin Deployments: Read
- Case Managers: Read, Edit
- Logistics: N/A
- Site Quality: Read
- System Support: Read
- Read Only Case Manager: Read
- Read Only Logistics: N/A
- Accession: N/A
- Integration: N/A
- HCP: N/A
- HCP Restricted: N/A
- Referring Physician: N/A

---

**Step 7**

**Description:**
Navigate to Object Manager > Treatment Case > Page Layouts. Open Care Program Enrollee Layout and verify the fields placed on the page layout.

**Expected Result:**
The Name and Role fields associated with Cancellation Requested By should not be displayed on the Treatment Case page layout.

---

**Step 8**

**Description:**
Log in as a Case Manager, open an ex-US Treatment Case record and verify the fields displayed on the Treatment Case page layout.

**Expected Result:**
The Name and Role fields associated with Cancellation Requested By should not be displayed on the Treatment Case page layout.
